iOS keyboard inset: the docked keyboard's part over the window, animated with the keyboard.

What: gpui_ios set `WindowInsets::ime.bottom` to the raw height of `UIKeyboardFrameEndUserInfoKey`, not intersected
with the view, so floating, undocked and split iPad keyboards, Split View, Slide Over and Stage Manager windows got
a wrong inset, and it jumped to the end frame although the trait asks to follow the animation. New
`keyboard_inset.rs` decides on plain values, as Flutter's `KeyboardInsetManager.swift`: notifications from another
app (`isLocal` false) and a dragged keyboard's zero frame are ignored; the end frame is docked, floating or hidden;
Slide Over's offset is added; the inset is the docked frame intersected with the view in the screen's coordinate
space; a new target starts an animation, a same-direction change while one runs continues it, and a hide with no
duration right after a show (the password manager's prompt) drops it to 0 at once. `window.rs` observes
`UIKeyboardWillShow` / `WillChangeFrame` / `WillHide` (was: WillChangeFrame and WillHide), answers the geometry
(`convertRect:toCoordinateSpace:` the screen's, `isPadInSlideOverOrStageManagerMode`), animates a hidden view's `y`
with the notification's duration as Flutter does, and when UIKit animates it with a `CASpringAnimation` (the
keyboard's curve) each display-link frame (`request_frame`, now given the link's `targetTimestamp`) sets the inset to
that spring at the frame's target time (new `spring_animation.rs`), frame-exact; without a spring it reads the view's
presentation layer. The completion of the animation still running sets the target. Table tests
`keyboard_inset::tests` (one row per keyboard case of FlutterViewControllerTest.mm, plus the spring's) and
`spring_animation::tests` (SpringAnimationTest.mm) run on the host (scripts/patch-test.sh, `ios-pure`).

Ported from flutter/flutter engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/darwin/ios/framework/Source/KeyboardInsetManager.swift,
FlutterViewController.mm (keyboard notifications, `isPadInSlideOverOrStageManagerMode`, `convertViewRectToScreen:`)
and the keyboard test cases of FlutterViewControllerTest.mm @ 3.50.1 (ae9b586f34a8443573f82ef57c3bf914a908cbf7).
Copyright 2014 The Flutter Authors. BSD-3-Clause, see third_party/flutter/LICENSE. The spring: ported from
flutter/flutter engine/src/flutter/third_party/spring_animation/spring_animation.mm and SpringAnimationTest.mm @ 3.50.1,
derived from facebook/react-native Libraries/Animated/animations/SpringAnimation.js
@ 494c47360f62761176033a4da359f43b53c2182f. Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates. MIT, see
LICENSE-REACT-NATIVE (GPUI's `SpringConfig` cannot stand in: it treats the keyboard's spring as overdamped and lags
far behind it, where Flutter's curve takes the critically damped branch). Left out: the `VSyncClient`
(the display link already ticks every frame), the engine view-controller check (each window observes for itself).
Changed: lengths are points, not physical pixels.

Why: apps lay out above the keyboard from `WindowInsets::ime`; a wrong or jumping inset leaves a gap under a floating
keyboard or a field hidden behind a docked one. The observers and inset are private to gpui_ios, so neither a
Parallax crate nor an extension trait can change them. cfg: the crate's own (iOS).

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

